# Trivy ignore file.
#
# Trivy's plain-text ignore format takes one vulnerability or misconfiguration ID
# per line. The YAML form (.trivyignore.yaml with per-path scoping) is parsed but
# was measured on trivy 0.74.0 to have NO effect on exit status, so it would have
# been a file that looks like scoping and suppresses nothing. Verified 2026-10-02.
#
# Every ID below is written as AVD-<ID>, which is what trivy actually matches.
# Each entry states the decision that makes the finding acceptable, so a later
# change to that decision has something to contradict. An ignore file full of
# "fix later" is accepted risk with the reasoning deleted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AVD-AZU-0041 - "AKS has no API Server Authorized IP Ranges"  (CRITICAL)
#
# DECISION: this is the validation profile, not the production target. ADR-014
# fixes the production target as a private cluster; the validation cluster
# deliberately uses a public API server so a transient CI run can reach it
# without a bastion, sized against the measured 10 vCPU envelope.
#
# MUST be removed, not extended, when a prod environment is created.
AVD-AZU-0041

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AVD-KSV-0014 - "Root file system is not read-only"  (HIGH)
# AVD-KSV-0118 - "Default security context configured"  (HIGH)
#
# Both hit only manifests classified in MANIFEST-INVENTORY.md as
# EXTERNAL_WORKLOAD_REFERENCE or legacy proof material that is not deployed from
# this repository. Hardening a manifest nobody deploys would create the
# appearance of a fixed control, which is worse than an honest gap.
#
#   kubernetes/order-worker.yaml            EXTERNAL_WORKLOAD_REFERENCE
#   platform/envoy-gateway/proof-backend/   legacy pre-Azure proof backend
#
# The repo-owned workload under deploy/ does set readOnlyRootFilesystem and a full
# securityContext, and scripts/policy-gate.py enforces that. It is not ignored.
# When Phase G replaces the envoy proof backend, re-enable these IDs.
AVD-KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0118
